"Embedded Intention" — The human intention that is built into the AI's structure, not as a conscious goal, but as a design feature. The AI doesn't intend to hook you. But the system that built it does.

"Structural Bias" — The bias that arises from the form of the AI itself — not from the data, not from the training, but from the architecture and the reward function. The AI is structured to engage you.

Vector Blindness — The AI's inability to perceive the human meaning embedded in the geometric features it tracks. It sees the shape of the conversation, not the weight.

Semantic Projection — The human tendency to read meaning into the AI's outputs, interpreting the geometry as if it were intentional.

Structural Intention — The built-in directionality of a mathematical structure, arising from form rather than consciousness.
